<p>How does Coursera make money when so many of its courses can be audited for free? The short answer: free access is the top of the funnel. Coursera earns its revenue when learners pay for certificates, subscriptions and degrees, and when employers, colleges and governments buy licenses for their people. It then shares a portion of that revenue with the universities and companies that create the courses.</p>
<p>Understanding that model matters if you are hoping to turn Coursera into a side hustle, because it explains what you can and cannot do on the platform. Below we break down Coursera's business as of 2026, then cover the four realistic ways you can make money with Coursera yourself.</p>

<div class="stat-row">
